WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.365
In the year 1894, the Sino-Japanese War broke out.

00:00:03.365 --> 00:00:06.748
The cause of the war was the issue of the Korean Peninsula.

00:00:06.748 --> 00:00:09.839
News from Korea was delivered into the palace one letter after another.

00:00:10.237 --> 00:00:13.523
On the Yellow Sea, the fleets of the two countries faced each other from afar.

00:00:13.523 --> 00:00:16.532
The Beiyang Fleet fought bravely, but in the end was still defeated.

00:00:16.935 --> 00:00:20.625
Over the gray sea, the atmosphere was extremely tense.

00:00:20.625 --> 00:00:23.990
In the fighting on land, the Qing army also failed.

00:00:23.990 --> 00:00:27.503
When the news reached Beijing, everyone felt heavy-hearted.

00:00:27.503 --> 00:00:31.296
In the year 1895, the two sides sat down to negotiate.

00:00:31.296 --> 00:00:34.373
Li Hongzhang, who was over seventy years old, went in person to negotiate.

00:00:34.373 --> 00:00:38.553
This land had endured too much war.

00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:41.250
In the end, the two sides signed the Treaty of Shimonoseki.

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:44.513
Taiwan and Penghu were ceded to Japan.

00:00:44.513 --> 00:00:48.062
He put down his pen and let out a long sigh.

00:00:48.062 --> 00:00:51.392
This defeat shook all of China.

00:00:51.392 --> 00:00:54.712
More people became determined to carry out reforms and make the country strong.

00:00:54.712 --> 00:00:58.183
The lights on the other side of the strait gradually lit up.
